        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Marc Vef",
          "email": "mvef@whamcloud.com",
          "date": "2026-08-24 13:29:08.000000000",
          "tz": 120
        },
        "subject": "LU-20565 tests: lower required OSTCOUNT for sanity-ec/7d",
        "message": "LU-20565 tests: lower required OSTCOUNT for sanity-ec/7d\n\nThe FLR layout for the test file in sanity-ec/7d currently requires 8\nOSTs. The OSTCOUNT check, however, only checks for 6. Patch testing\nfor sanity-ec runs in a configuration where 8 OSTs are available. In\nfull (full-part-3) testing for master and master-next, it is run with\n7 OSTs causing the file create to fail on mirror creation with ENOSPC.\n\nFor test 7d such a complex layout is not needed since it is only about\nthe number of mirrors. Therefore, reduce the OST requirements of the\ntest, so that 7d can run in environments with fewer OSTs.\n\nFixes: dfb93e4978 (\"LU-19548 lfs: mirror split -d for parity mirrors\")\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nTest-Parameters: testlist=sanity-ec ostcount=6\nTest-Parameters: testlist=sanity-ec ostcount=7\nSigned-off-by: Marc Vef <mvef@whamcloud.com>\nChange-Id: I66a3672905b745def41f63c7c08b28542e127cc9\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
